Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final  Type  Surgical Pathology  Pathology Report  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  BREAST MASTECTOMY   PARTIAL OR SIMPLE  Accessioned On  REMOVED_DATE  WELCH  WILLIAM  ROBERT  M D   DIAGNOSIS  by WELCH WILLIAM ROBERT M D   RIGHT BREAST  SIMPLE MASTECTOMY   ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  See note   Florid epithelial hyperplasia   Microcalcifications are present in association with the epithelial  hyperplasia and atypical ductal hyperplasia   Sclerosing adenosis   Biopsy site with repair reaction   Cicatrix   Three lymph nodes  no significant pathologic change   NOTE  The atypical ductal hyperplasia arises in the context of a florid  proliferative epithelial changes  the atypia does not quite satisfy  criteria for DCIS  levels examined    CLINICAL DATA   History  History of DCIS in two quadrants  right upper and right medial  lower quadrant   Clinical Diagnosis  DCIS   TISSUE SUBMITTED   1  Right breast  stitch marks axillary tail    GROSS DESCRIPTION  by DEBNATH JAYANTA M D   The specimen is received fresh  in one  1  part  labeled with the patient s  name  unit number  and  right breast   and consists of a right simple  mastectomy specimen weighing 895 grams and measuring 26 x 18 x 6 5cm  There is  a white tan skin ellipse  19 x 13cm   with two  2  well healed surgical  scars The first scar is in the lower inner quadrant  4 5cm in length   and REMOVED_DATE  cm from an unremarkable nipple  The second is in the lower outer quadrant   4 5cm    and is located 5cm from an unremarkable 1cm nipple  There is a  stitch that marks a short axillary tail and corresponds to level 1 lymph nodes   3 x 5 x 1 0cm    The deep margin is inked in black  and consists of smooth  fascia  except for a surgical tear measuring 4 x 2cm  which opens into a  hollow cavity  Sectioning of the breast parenchyma reveals a large biopsy  cavity  red pink in color  and measuring 12 x 4 x 4cm  The biopsy cavity is  grossly 0 1cm from the inked deep margin and