rogen receptor  progesterone receptor  and Her2 neu will be attempted and the results will be reported in an addendum  SKIN  LEFT BREAST ADDITIONAL   EXCISION  SKIN AND SUBCUTANEOUS FAT WITH FAT NECROSIS  HEMORRHAGE  AND FIBROSIS  BREAST  RIGHT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  MILDLY ATYPICAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  COLUMNAR CELL TYPE  SCATTERED FOCI  MILD FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  PSEUDOANGIOMATOUS STROMAL HYPERPLASIA  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 3 OF 3 AXILLARY LYMPH NODES  LYMPH NODE  RIGHT AXILLA  SENTINEL   EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 2 OF 2 LYMPH NODES  SEE NOTE   NOTE  Keratin positive tumor cells are not identified on three  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  3 Cam5 2 immunostained levels  SKIN  RIGHT BREAST ADDITIONAL   EXCISION  NO DIAGNOSTIC ABNORMALITY  By his her signature below  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh  labeled with the patient s name  unit number  and  right breast   is an 850 gram  26 x 18 x 3 5cm simple mastectomy specimen with axillary tail measuring 5 x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm  There is a 4 x 3cm skin ellipse centered around the nipple on the anterior surface  The anterior surface is dark yellow  fatty with no areas of puckering  The posterior surface is yellow red  smooth and glistening  The anterior resection margin is inked blue  the posterior resection margin is inked black  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal predominantly dense fibrous breast tissue surrounded peripherally by yellow unremarkable fat  No discrete lesions or otherwise suspicious areas are identified  The axillary tail is dissected to reveal three potential lymph nodes  Representative sections of the breast parenchyma including the deep margin are submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   The three potential lymph nodes are submitted as  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received in formalin  labeled with the patient s name  unit num